  "training": {
    "hints": [
      "Define the required result before writing logic: Transfer begins only after both spindles are home; all motion commands finish off.",
      "Rotation uses drill_a_run/drill_b_run. Independently command each drill_*_feed or drill_*_retract; simultaneous feed/retract holds position. Feed requires rotation and the fixture at home. Read drill_*_home and drill_*_at_depth from actual simulated travel. Transfer requires both heads home and both rotation commands off.",
      "Use a step/state approach and prove the transition order: parallel drilling \u2192 spindle dwell \u2192 retracting \u2192 both home \u2192 transfer plate \u2192 complete."
    ],
    "solution": {
      "summary": "This is one valid functional reference. The same behavior may be implemented in LAD, FBD, or SCL; the rung layout is not prescribed.",
      "steps": [
        "Command both rotation outputs and both feed outputs; wait for both at_depth inputs.",
        "Remove feed requests and dwell as required by the exercise.",
        "Command each retract independently; wait for both home inputs.",
        "Remove retract and rotation commands, then extend transfer; wait for transfer_at_end.",
        "Remove transfer_extend to hold the supported endpoint. Command transfer_retract only when a return is required; contradictory transfer requests hold."
      ],
      "acceptance": "Transfer begins only after both spindles are home; all motion commands finish off."
    },
    "machineGuide": {
      "purpose": "Two drill heads process a clamped plate in parallel, retract independently, and release a transfer slide only after both are home.",
      "startConditions": [
        "The common PLC/watchdog foundation is healthy.",
        "All required simulator inputs are at their documented initial state.",
        "The PLC commands rotation, feed/retract and transfer separately. Native feed/return durations are 1.7/1.6 s for 330 mm travel; transfer is 1.2 s for 2.2 m travel. These are simulator settings, not physical machine specifications."
      ],
      "normalSequence": [
        "parallel drilling",
        "spindle dwell",
        "retracting",
        "both home",
        "transfer plate",
        "complete"
      ],
      "stopBehavior": [
        "A normal stop removes PLC-owned commands and leaves the equipment in a safe state.",
        "Reset returns the scene to its documented initial condition."
      ],
      "faultBehavior": [
        "A missing, stale, or incorrectly typed input must not be replaced by simulator logic.",
        "A missing PLC command leaves the affected equipment stopped and the test diagnosable."
      ],
      "expectedObservations": [
        "Transfer begins only after both spindles are home; all motion commands finish off."
      ]
    },
